 "verdict": "partly consistent: the group after مدنف reads كييب by recurrent shapes, against كيف in the verse.",
 "notes": "The disputed group visibly contains a ring, two identically oriented stemmed loops, and a double arch. The ring is kāf in فكم and كتاب, the stemmed loop is yāʾ in على and يطلب, and the double arch is bāʾ in خطاب and كتاب. The usual fāʾ is a plain peak in مدنف and فكم. The last hamza in انتهاء lacks its own sign. The two differences compensate in the overall count.",
